# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this template is not.
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The harness passes these through to the container automatically.

# Which adapter runs: nvidia (default) | anthropic
AGENT_PROVIDER=nvidia

# NVIDIA NIM - free key, no credit card, no expiry: https://build.nvidia.com
NVIDIA_API_KEY=

# Optional overrides. Tool-calling reliability varies a lot between open-weight
# models, and there is no fallback if it is poor, so change this if the probe in
# Phase B task B9 shows the default cannot hold a multi-turn loop.
# NIM_MODEL=meta/llama-3.1-70b-instruct
# NIM_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1

# Anthropic path, used when AGENT_PROVIDER=anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local models via Ollama - NOT the scored configuration.
#
# Kept for three jobs: a fallback when the free tier refuses, rig testing that
# burns no quota, and running the scored suite with networking fully off (the
# container then needs only the host, never the internet).
#
# Measured on a 4GB-VRAM laptop, not assumed: qwen2.5:7b holds tool calling for
# a few turns and then leaks raw <tool_call> markup as message text, which this
# architecture cannot recover from because parsing calls out of free text is
# forbidden. llama3.2:3b stops calling tools after one turn. Re-measure before
# baselining on either.
#
# The context length MUST be pinned. A default 128K window allocates a ~13.5GB
# KV cache up front, and the server dies with an error naming a buffer size
# rather than a context setting - unguessable from the message alone:
#     printf 'FROM qwen2.5:7b\nPARAMETER num_ctx 8192\n' > Modelfile
#     ollama create agent-qwen25:7b -f Modelfile
#
# AGENT_PROVIDER=openai
# NIM_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
# NIM_MODEL=agent-qwen25:7b
# OPENAI_API_KEY=ollama        # any non-empty string: required, never used
